2026-03-09T23:57:13.0025932Z  > {"github_actor":"tonistiigi","github_actor_id":"585223","github_event_name":"push","github_event_payload":{"after":"a5f49f0c1767e0e24fc43a3845ec71524995035b","base_ref":null,"before":"c423bc738b1178cda935006940eb0216ba745629","commits":[{"author":{"email":"tonistiigi@gmail.com","name":"Tonis Tiigi","username":"tonistiigi"},"committer":{"email":"tonistiigi@gmail.com","name":"Tonis Tiigi","username":"tonistiigi"},"distinct":false,"id":"2adc53cfb3e2718eec66c9b82d15387e390a3b17","message":"build: parallelize forced reference evaluation\n\nUse an errgroup helper to evaluate result refs concurrently during forced\nevaluation, and fail fast on the first evaluation error.\n\nThis mitigates current case in bake where chained targets with\na multi-platform build could miss secrets and other session properties.\n\nThe outline for the issue case:\n- Base target is solved but only lazily and not really loaded/tracked\nin build graph yet.\n- Child targets are loaded, base target waits.\n- Evaluate is called for base stage (because it might be missing result\ncondition), child stage is processed as build result. This happens in\nparallel.\n- Because `Evaluate()` was called synchronously, it may have not been\n called yet for the second platform while the child target already\n needs to run `RUN --mount=type=secret`.\n\nSigned-off-by: Tonis Tiigi \u003ctonistiigi@gmail.com\u003e","timestamp":"2026-03-04T18:09:41-08:00","tree_id":"e9d8c60a4c7237df9d23dc31163933c99c0a3250","url":"https://github.com/docker/buildx/commit/2adc53cfb3e2718eec66c9b82d15387e390a3b17"},{"author":{"email":"tonistiigi@gmail.com","name":"Tõnis Tiigi","username":"tonistiigi"},"committer":{"email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub","username":"web-flow"},"distinct":true,"id":"a5f49f0c1767e0e24fc43a3845ec71524995035b","message":"Merge pull request #3696 from tonistiigi/bake-linked-target-fix\n\nbuild: parallelize forced reference evaluation","timestamp":"2026-03-09T16:44:38-07:00"